Findings from reviewing the compare branch (`convert-full-transcript...convert-full-transcript-agent-support`) ([GitHub compare](https://github.com/entireio/cli/compare/convert-full-transcript...convert-full-transcript-agent-support)):

- **High – Test suite currently fails because `droid_test.go` expects an output type that the implementation never emits.**  
  `TestCompact_FactoryDroidInlineCases/tool result` expects a `user_tool_result` line, but shared compaction only emits `user` and `assistant` and drops tool-result-only user entries after inlining/processing.  
  This is reproducible with `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact -count=1` (fails at that subtest).

```29:36:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/droid_test.go
name: "tool result",
// Droid user message with tool_result blocks inside the envelope.
input: []byte(`{"type":"message","id":"m1","timestamp":"t1","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"tu-1","content":"success"},{"type":"text","text":"next step"}]}}
`),
expected: []string{
	`{"v":1,"agent":"factoryai-droid","cli_version":"0.5.1","type":"user","ts":"t1","content":"next step"}`,
	`{"v":1,"agent":"factoryai-droid","cli_version":"0.5.1","type":"user_tool_result","ts":"t1","tool_use_id":"tu-1","result":{}}`,
},
```

```179:187:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/compact.go
case transcript.TypeUser:
	// User entries that are purely tool results were already consumed
	// by the assistant look-ahead above. If we reach one here it was
	// not preceded by an assistant with a matching tool_use, so emit
	// it only if it has text content.
	if e.toolUseID != "" && e.userText == "" {
		continue
	}
	emitUser(&result, meta, e)
```

- **Medium – `inlineToolResult` can attach a result to a non-`tool_use` block when no matching `tool_use` exists.**  
  The index defaults to `len(blocks)-1`; if no `tool_use` is found/matched, `result` is still written to that last block. That can corrupt content structure (e.g., result added onto a text/image block).

```331:352:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/compact.go
// Find the tool_use block matching the user's tool_use_id (or the last one).
idx := len(blocks) - 1
for i := len(blocks) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {
	if unquote(blocks[i]["type"]) == transcript.ContentTypeToolUse {
		if user.toolUseID == "" || unquote(blocks[i]["id"]) == user.toolUseID {
			idx = i
			break
		}
	}
}
...
blocks[idx]["result"] = resultObj
```

- **Medium – Test scope duplication remains in `compact_test.go` and overlaps with agent-specific behavior tests.**  
  Inlining behavior is validated multiple times with very similar setup/expectations. This makes intent noisier and maintenance heavier.

```78:86:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/compact_test.go
func TestCompact_UserWithToolResult(t *testing.T) {
	t.Parallel()
	...
	assertJSONLines(t, result, expected)
}
```

```239:247:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/compact_test.go
func TestCompact_ToolResultInlinedIntoPrecedingAssistant(t *testing.T) {
	t.Parallel()
	...
	result, err := Compact(input, defaultOpts)
```

- **Low – Agent fixture strategy is still inconsistent with your stated direction.**  
  Gemini/OpenCode use `*_full.jsonl` -> `*_expected.jsonl` fixture assertions, but Droid still uses inline cases only.

```7:10:cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/gemini_test.go
